# Round XXIX Track A: `s[0]` on a `HashSet[T]` REJECTS at check-time with
# `E_NotIndexable`. Sibling of `set_index_returns_garbage.gg` — Set and
# HashSet are separate collection kinds (`CollectionKind::OrderedSet` vs
# `CollectionKind::Set`), pinning both cells guards against a future arm
# that re-adds only ONE. D38 ratifies: no lookup key on a Set-family type.
#
# Pre-fix: silent-accept + garbage read (same class as Set[int]).
# Post-fix: rejects with E_NotIndexable (HashSet is NOT in
# `is_indexable_intrinsic`).
int main():
    HashSet[int] s = HashSet[int]()
    s.add(42)
    int x = s[0]
    print(x)
    return 0
